    {
      "entity_id": "surya-claim-r2-single-stressor-inventory-2026-08",
      "evidence_class": "evidence-backed",
      "kind": "claim",
      "local_ref": "c2",
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "title": "R2 single-stressor inventory (Aug 2026): radiation evidence is strong (1 MeV electrons to 1e16 e/cm2 no loss; protons tolerated to ~1e13 p/cm2 with in-situ self-healing; failure at 3e14 p/cm2 via transport-layer breakdown); UV thin (800 h narrowband 365 nm max, no AM0-calibrated dose); ATOX nearly absent (one 120-min plasma study, not fluence-calibrated); LEO-range thermal cycling absent (widest tested -60/+80 C x 120 cycles vs required ~-120/+120 C x thousands)"
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "surya-claim-r2-qualification-benchmark-2026-08",
      "evidence_class": "evidence-backed",
      "kind": "claim",
      "local_ref": "c3",
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "title": "R2 qualification benchmark (Aug 2026): a credible 5-year LEO degradation model by incumbent practice requires DDD/equivalent-fluence reducibility of radiation data, mission-spectrum convolution (SAVANT/SPENVIS class), EOL prediction validated against flight data, and an S-111/S-112-class test matrix (~$4.5M, 1-2+ years per campaign); ECSS-E-ST-20-08C currently excludes thin-film cells entirely"
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "surya-claim-r2-gap-shape-2026-08",
      "evidence_class": "evidence-backed",
      "kind": "claim",
      "local_ref": "c4",
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "title": "R2 gap shape (Aug 2026): the coupled-stressor gap decomposes into four fillable datasets - LEO-range thermal-vacuum cycling with IV monitoring; AM0-calibrated UV dose; ATOX fluence-calibrated exposure; and a combined in-situ campaign (radiation + thermal cycling + AM0 + vacuum). Combined-exposure facilities exist (NASA Glenn, MSFC, ESA/ESTEC, DLR) but none has published a perovskite PV campaign"
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "surya-claim-r2-gap-map-2026-08",
      "evidence_class": "evidence-backed",
      "kind": "claim",
      "local_ref": "c1",
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "title": "R2 gap map (Aug 2026): the coupled-stressor gap is real and total - no published ground study combines particle radiation with thermal cycling, and no 3+ space-stressor simultaneous perovskite experiment exists; combined-stressor data exists only as flight data without stressor attribution (MISSE 10-month, CubeSats ~100 days); the 2025-2026 review literature states this gap explicitly"
    },
